ClockLaneLP2HSTime|Maximum time taken by the D-PHY clock lane to go from LP to HS transmission|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|lane byte clock cycles|0|1023|LP2HS = TLPX_CLK + TCLK_PREPARE + TCLK_ZERO
ClockLaneLP2HSTime_ns|Resulting Maximum time taken by the D-PHY clock lane to go from LP to HS transmission|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|ns|||
ClockLaneHS2LPTime|Maximum time taken by the D-PHY clock lane to go from HS to LP transmission|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|lane byte clock cycles|0|1023|HS2LP = TCLK_POST + TCLK_TRAIL + TCLK_EXIT TCLK_TRAIL=60ns TCLK_EXIT=100ns
ClockLaneHS2LPTime_ns|Resulting Maximum time taken by the D-PHY clock lane to go from HS to LP transmission|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|ns|||
DataLaneHS2LPTime|Maximum time taken by the D-PHY data lane to go from HS to LP transmission|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|lane byte clock cycles|0|255|HS2LP = THS_TRAIL + THS_EXIT
DataLaneHS2LPTime_ns|Resulting Maximum time taken by the D-PHY data lane to go from HS to LP transmission|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|ns|||
DataLaneLP2HSTime|Maximum time taken by the D-PHY data lane to go from LP to HS transmission|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|lane byte clock cycles|0|255|LP2HS = TLPX_DATA + THS_PREPARE + THS_ZERO
DataLaneLP2HSTime_ns|Resulting Maximum time taken by the D-PHY data lane to go from LP to HS transmission|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|ns|||
DataLaneMaxReadTime|Maximum time taken to perform a read command|Read Command Timing|lane byte clock cycles|0|32767|The MRD_TIME field is used in LP mode to determine if there is time to complete a read command in a BLLP period. MRD_TIME = Time to transmit the read command in LP mode + Time to enter and leave LPmode + Time to return the read data packet from the peripheral device. MRD_TIME = (tHS2LP + tLP2HS + tread + 2tBTA) / lanebyteclkperiod. Timings are expressed in ns. tHS2LP = time to enter the LP mode. tLP2HS = time to leave the LP mode. tLPDT = D-PHY timing related to Escape mode entry, LPDT command, and Escape mode exit (according to the D-PHY specification, this value is always 11 bits in LP. tlprd = Read command time in LP mode (64 * TX esc clock). tread = Time to return the read data packet from the peripheral. tBTA = time to perform a bus turnaround (D-PHY dependent).
DataLaneMaxReadTime_ns|Resulting Maximum time taken to perform a read command|Read Command Timing|ns|||
StopWaitTime|Minimum wait period to request a HS transmission after the Stop state (min est 1 cycle de escape clock)|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|lane byte clock cycles|0|255|
StopWaitTime_ns|Resulting Minimum wait period to request a HS transmission after the Stop state (min est 1 cycle de escape clock)|LP to HS and HS to LP Transitions Timings|ns|||
HighSpeedClockfromDSI_noparam|High Speed Clock - PLLDSI Output|from PLLDSI|kHz|||
LaneByteClockfromDSI_noparam|Lane Byte Clock|from PLLDSI|kHz|||
LaneByteClockfromPLLR_noparam|Lane Byte Clock|from PLL3P|kHz|||
TransmissionEscapeClockfromDSI_noparam|Transmission Escape Clock|from PLLDSI|kHz|||
TransmissionEscapeClockfromPLLR_noparam|Transmission Escape Clock|from PLL3P|kHz|||
EscapeClockDivider_noparam|Escape Clock Divider|from PLLDSI||||
TimeOutClockfromDSI_noparam|Time Out Clock|from PLLDSI|kHz|||
TimeOutClockfromDSI_noparamfortimeout|Time Out Clock - from PLLDSI|Time Out Clock Setting|kHz|||
TimeOutClockfromPLLR_noparam|Time Out Clock|from PLL3P|kHz|||
TimeoutCkdiv|Time Out Clock Divider|Time Out Clock Setting||1|256|
Mode|Video Mode|Video Mode Configuration||||The Burst mode increases the probability of the link spending more time in low-power mode: the DSI output bandwidth should be higher than the LTDC input bandwidth in a relation that enables the link to go to low-power once per line. The condition to use BURST mode is that the display device should support receiving a full pixel line in a single packet burst; if not use the Non Burst Mode
PacketSize|Video Packet Size|Video Mode Configuration|Pixels|1|8191|The video packet size is limited by the size of the Pixel FIFO inside the display device. For 18-bit not loosely packed data types, this number must be a multiple of 4
NumberOfChunks|Number of Chuncks|Video Mode Configuration||0|8191|The pixel line is divided into several chunks of Video Packet Size pixels . If set to 0 or 1, the video line is transmitted in a single packet. If set to 1, the packet is part of a chunk, so a null packet follows it if Null Packet SIZE > 0. You must set the value to have Video Packet Size * Number of Chuncks = Number of Pixels per Line
NullPacketSize|Null Packet Size|Video Mode Configuration|Bytes|0|8191|Each chunk is composed of Video Packet Size pixels followed by Null Packet Size in a way that LTDC interface input pixel ratio matches with the DSI output pixel ratio. If Null Packet are allowed, the following equation has to be verified : lanebyteclkperiod * Number_of_Chuncks (VideoPacketSize * bytes_per_pixel + 12 + NullPacketSize) / number_of_lanes = pixels_per_line * LTDC_Clock_period If Null Packet are not allowed, the following equation has to be verified : lanebyteclkperiod * Number_of_Chuncks (VideoPacketSize * bytes_per_pixel + 6) / number_of_lanes = pixels_per_line * LTDC_Clock_period
LPHorizontalFrontPorchEnable|Horizontal Front-Porch (HFP) Period|Enabling Low-Power Transitions during:||||
LPHorizontalBackPorchEnable|Horizontal Back-Porch (HBP) Period|Enabling Low-Power Transitions during:||||
LPVerticalActiveEnable|Vertical Active (VACT) Period|Enabling Low-Power Transitions during:||||
LPVerticalFrontPorchEnable|Vertical Front Porch (VFP) Period|Enabling Low-Power Transitions during:||||
LPVerticalBackPorchEnable|Vertical Back Porch (VBP) Period|Enabling Low-Power Transitions during:||||
LPVerticalSyncActiveEnable|Vertical Sync time (VSA) Period|Enabling Low-Power Transitions during:||||
LPCommandEnable|During HS Video Mode, Commands are Transmited in|Transmission of Commands during HS Video Transmission Mode||||If the commands are sent in high-speed in Video mode, the DSI Host automatically determines the area where each command can be sent and no programming or calculation is required.
LPLargestPacketSize|The size of the LP largest packet that can fit in a line during VSA, VBP and VFP regions|Maximum Size allowed for Commands (except Read Command)|Bytes|0|255|The LPSIZE field is compared directly with the size of the command to be transmitted to determine if there is time to transmit the command. LPSIZE = (tL - (tH1 + tHS2LP + tLP2HS + tLPDT + 2 tESCCLK)) / (2.8.tESCCLK). Timings are expressed in ns. tL = line time. tH1 = time of the HSA pulse for sync pulses mode or time to send the HSS packet, including EoTp. tHS2LP = time to enter the LP mode. tLP2HS = time to leave the LP mode. tLPDT = D-PHY timing related with Escape mode Entry, LPDT Command, and Escape Exit. According to the D-PHY specification, this value is always 11 bits in LP. tESCCLK = escape clock period the term 2 tESCCLK is a delay imposed by the DSI Host implementation. The division by (2.8.tESCCLK) allows to expressed LPSIZE in number of Bytes transfered using the Escape Clock where 1 byte is transmitted every 2 cycles
LPVACTLargestPacketSize|The size of the LP largest packet that can fit in a line during VACT region|Maximum Size allowed for Commands (except Read Command)|Bytes|0|255|The VLPSIZE field is compared directly with the size of the command to be transmitted to determine if there is time to transmit the command. VLPSIZE = (tL - (tHSA + tHBP + tHACT + tHS2LP + tLP2HS + tLPDT + 2 tESCCLK))/(2 . 8 . tESCCLK). Timings are expressed in ns. tL = line time. tHSA = time of the HSA pulse. tHBP = time of Horizontal back porch. tHACT = time of Video active. For Burst mode, the Video active is time compressed and is calculated as tHACT = (VPSIZE.Bytes_per_Pixel/Number_Lanes).tlanebyteclock tlanebyteclock = lane byte clock period tESCCLK = escape clock period tHS2LP = time to enter the LP mode. tLP2HS = time to leave the LP mode. tLPDT = D-PHY timing related with Escape mode Entry, LPDT Command, and Escape Exit. According to the D-PHY specification, this value is always 11 bits in LP. The division by (2.8.tESCCLK) allows to expressed LPSIZE in number of Bytes transfered using the Escape Clock where 1 byte is transmitted every 2 cycles
